            "rider_1_name": "Billy Ottervanger",
            "rider_1_role": "Owner",
            "rider_1_image": "shopify://shop_images/IMG_3876.jpg",
            "rider_1_bio": "<p>Hi, I’m Billy Ottervanger, also known as Oshow, and I’m the owner of Crew Racewear.<br/><br/>Motocross has always been, and will always be, one of my greatest passions in life. When we started Crew Racewear, we wanted to create something that went beyond high quality motocross gear. Our vision was to build a community of riders who support one another, make a positive impact on the sport, and believe in being part of something bigger than themselves.<br/><br/>Crew isn’t just a brand it’s a community. When you see a Crew banner at the track, we want you to know you’re surrounded by people you can count on, whether you need a helping hand, someone to line up beside, or simply a place where you belong.<br/><br/>That’s what Crew Racewear represents: great gear, great people, and a community built around the sport we love.</p>",
            "rider_2_name": "Haley Ottervanger",
            "rider_2_role": "Co-Owner",
            "rider_2_image": "shopify://shop_images/image_a285bb9b-efa4-4e8a-9bce-72b84a374887.jpg",
            "rider_2_bio": "",
            "rider_3_name": "Ethan Paltan",
            "rider_3_role": "Co-Owner // Graphics designer",
            "rider_3_image": "shopify://shop_images/sleepy_1.jpg",
            "rider_3_bio": "<p>I’m Ethan, a co-owner of Crew Racewear. I’m married and have a huge passion for motocross, graphic design, and creating something different. Crew Racewear gives me the opportunity to combine my love for the sport with my creativity and help build a brand riders are proud to represent.</p>",
            "rider_4_name": "Kevin Sampey",
            "rider_4_role": "Web Designer",
            "rider_4_image": "shopify://shop_images/IMG_8983.jpg",
            "rider_4_bio": "<p>How's it going! I'm Kevin, and I'm the web designer for Crew Racewear. I've been racing motocross for the past 21 years. Louisiana native and United States Marine Corps Veteran.</p>",
            "rider_5_name": "Nick Castillo",
            "rider_5_role": "Media-Editor",
            "rider_5_image": "shopify://shop_images/IMG_5736.jpg",
            "rider_5_bio": "",
            "rider_6_name": "Troy Vowell",
            "rider_6_role": "Graphics Designer",
            "rider_6_image": "shopify://shop_images/Troy_1.jpg",
            "rider_6_bio": "<p>Racing when he can, creating when he can’t. Troy Vowell is a Texas woods and motocross racer who also works on the creative side of Crew, bringing a rider’s perspective into graphics, gear, and new ideas for the brand</p>",
            "rider_7_name": "William Knau",
            "rider_7_role": "Graphics Designer",
            "rider_7_image": "shopify://shop_images/IMG_7991.jpg",
            "rider_7_bio": "<p>Local pro adobe product user c class racer</p>",
            "rider_8_name": "LEON TYE",
            "rider_8_role": "Marketing // Merchandise",
            "rider_8_image": "shopify://shop_images/IMG_7694.jpg",
            "rider_8_bio": "<p>I’m Leon Tye, a World Championship Sidecarcross passenger from the UK, as well as a graphic designer and video editor.<br/><br/>Racing has always been a big part of my life, but I’ve also always enjoyed the creative side of the sport — designing graphics, clothing and creating content around motocross. That’s something I’ve been able to turn into my work, and I’m now really happy to be working with CREW across their marketing and merch lines.<br/><br/>Coming from the sidecar world gives me a slightly different view of motocross. It’s a smaller, close-knit part of the sport with its own style and community, so I’ve grown up seeing things from a slightly different angle. I think that mix of being a rider, a designer and someone who enjoys creating things gives me a good way of bringing different ideas into what I do with CREW.</p>",
